    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So, based on your history, it's hard to say. An outer ear canal infection is one possibility and a middle ear infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet. I'll start you on antibiotic and steroid ear drops, 3 drops, twice a day, for seven days. It's for ear canal infection. Keep the ear dry, no swimming, and don't poke anything into it.",
